  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.25,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.12,
    "rationale": "I diluted the 18 h aliquot and scaled each reading back by its dilution factor. The undiluted reading was 1.209 (the 15–18 h readings were about 1.21–1.26). The scaled dilution readings were 1.255 at 4x, 1.35 at 10x (two replicates, 0.1325 and 0.1375), 1.254 at 20x and 1.076 at 40x. If the reader were saturating at the plateau, the scaled values would rise steadily as dilution increased, and they do not. They cluster around 1.25 without a trend. The 10x value is about 8% high and the 40x value about 14% low. Both fit read noise, because the 40x signal is only about 0.027 OD and is sensitive to a small blank offset. The plateau at about 1.22 therefore looks like real stationary-phase biomass and not a detector ceiling. The estimate of 1.25 is the average of the 4x and 20x scaled readings. I could not rule out a small saturation effect of a few percent."
  },
